 ('Reading · A film review',text('Review: “Words That Divide”',['This documentary asks why teams from different countries **fail to cooperate**. Its answer: not **hostility**, but habit. In one scene, a manager says, “Because they communicated poorly, the project failed.” The narrator rephrases: “**Poor communication** led to **the failure** of the project.” The second sentence sounds colder, yet more official.','The film’s strength is this contrast between speech and report. Its weakness is **repetition**: the same point is made four times. Still, **the clarity of its argument** and **the quality of its interviews** make it worth watching.'],kicker='REVIEW',by='Cine Notes',gloss=[('hostility','hostilidade'),('rephrase','reformular'),('cold','frio'),('repetition','repetição')])),
 [('The documentary blames hostility for the failure.','F','not hostility, but habit.'),('The narrator uses a more formal style than the manager.','T','sounds colder, yet more official.'),('The reviewer finds the film too short.','NG','extensão não é discutida.')],
 [('“rephrase” = ?',['reformular','repetir','frasear só'],0,'rephrase = reformular.'),('“repetition” = ?',['repetição','recepção','reputação'],0,'repetition = repetição.')],
 G('Estilo verbal × estilo nominal',['Verbal (mais falado)','Nominal (mais formal)'],[['Because they communicated poorly, the project failed.','**Poor communication** led to **the failure** of the project.'],['They decided quickly, so we saved time.','**Their quick decision** saved us time.'],['People protested because prices rose.','**The rise in prices** provoked **protest**.'],['We need to improve how we cooperate.','**An improvement in cooperation** is needed.']],'O estilo nominal usa **substantivos abstratos** como sujeito e verbos de ligação (*led to, resulted in, gave rise to*). É frequente em textos acadêmicos.','Não nominalize tudo: em fala e e-mails informais o estilo verbal soa mais natural.'),
 [('Poor ___ led to the failure. (communicate)','communication','nominalização.',None),('The ___ of the project surprised us. (fail)','failure','nominalização.',None),('The rise in prices ___ protest. (provoke)','provoked','verbo de ligação.',None),('Their quick ___ saved time. (decide)','decision','nominalização.',None)],
 V('documentary film=filme documentário|narrator’s voice=voz do narrador|interview footage=imagens de entrevistas|stylistic contrast=contraste estilístico|official register=registro oficial|spoken habit=hábito da fala|workplace habit=hábito de trabalho|cooperation problem=problema de cooperação|team conflict=conflito de equipe|poor communication=comunicação deficiente|reasoning quality=qualidade do raciocínio|film strength=ponto forte do filme|repeated point=ponto repetido|critic’s remark=comentário do crítico|rating system=sistema de notas|running time=duração do filme|opening sequence=sequência de abertura|closing credits=créditos finais|cultural documentary=documentário cultural|interviewee=entrevistado|cold tone=tom frio|clear structure=estrutura clara|film festival=festival de cinema|screening room=sala de exibição|audience reaction=reação do público|review score=nota da crítica|filmmaker’s intent=intenção do cineasta|script quality=qualidade do roteiro'),
 ('Film club',[('Ana','Which sentence sounds more official?','Qual frase soa mais oficial?'),('Leo','The nominal one: “Poor communication led to the failure.”','A nominal: “Poor communication led to the failure.”'),('Ana','Is it always better?','É sempre melhor?'),('Leo','No. In speech, verbs sound more natural.','Não. Na fala, verbos soam mais naturais.')]),
 [('Rephrase a verbal sentence.','Reformule.','Because they argued, we waited → Their argument delayed us.'),('Say when nominal style is appropriate.','Diga.','It suits reports and academic writing.'),('Give a verdict on a film.','Opine.','The clarity of its argument makes it worth seeing.')],
